# ===========================================
# OmniRoute Configuration
# ===========================================
# Unified AI Gateway for DigitallyDefined OS
# Replaces: GROQ_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, etc.

# Required: OmniRoute API Key
# Get your key from https://omniroute.ai
OMNIROUTE_API_KEY=sk-or-1-your-omniroute-api-key-here

# Optional: OmniRoute Base URL (default: https://omniroute.ai)
# Use this if you're self-hosting OmniRoute or using a custom endpoint
OMNIROUTE_BASE_URL=https://omniroute.ai

# Optional: Default Model (default: openai/gpt-4o-mini)
# Examples: openai/gpt-4o-mini, anthropic/claude-3-haiku, google/gemini-pro, etc.
OMNIROUTE_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# Optional: Fallback Models (comma-separated)
# These models will be tried in order if the primary model fails
# Example: anthropic/claude-3-haiku,google/gemini-pro
OMNIROUTE_FALLBACK_MODEL_1=anthropic/claude-3-haiku
OMNIROUTE_FALLBACK_MODEL_2=google/gemini-pro

# ===========================================
# AgentOps Monitoring (Optional but Recommended)
# ===========================================
# Get your API key from: https://app.agentops.ai/settings/projects
# AGENTOPS_API_KEY=your_agentops_api_key_here

# ===========================================
# Legacy API Keys (No Longer Required)
# ===========================================
# The following keys are NO LONGER NEEDED if using OmniRoute:
# - GROQ_API_KEY
# - OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# - OPENROUTER_MODEL
# - OPENAI_API_KEY
# - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# - GOOGLE_API_KEY
# - ZAI_API_KEY
# - NOUS_API_KEY
# 
# You can remove these from your environment once OmniRoute is configured.

# ===========================================
# Backend Configuration
# ===========================================
# These are still required for non-AI features:

# Dashboard API Key (for frontend authentication)
DASHBOARD_API_KEY=your-dashboard-api-key-here

# Notion Integration
NOTION_API_KEY=secret_your-notion-api-key
NOTION_IDEAS_DB_ID=your-ideas-database-id
NOTION_CONTENT_DB_ID=your-content-database-id
NOTION_AUTOMATIONS_DB_ID=your-automations-database-id
NOTION_COMMAND_CENTER_DB_ID=your-command-center-db-id
NOTION_PUBLISHING_QUEUE_DB_ID=your-publishing-queue-db-id
NOTION_CONTENT_APPROVALS_DB_ID=your-content-approvals-db-id
NOTION_BUYER_SIGNALS_DB_ID=your-buyer-signals-db-id
NOTION_AI_CONTENT_DRAFTS_DB_ID=your-ai-content-drafts-db-id
NOTION_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-webhook-secret

# Social Media APIs
FACEBOOK_GROUP_ID=your-facebook-group-id
FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-facebook-access-token

# Email Marketing
SENDPULSE_API_ID=your-sendpulse-api-id
SENDPULSE_API_SECRET=your-sendpulse-api-secret
BREVO_API_KEY=your-brevo-api-key
BREVO_LIST_ID=2

# Google Sheets
SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-sheets-webhook-url.com

# Antigravity (optional)
ANTIGRAVITY_API_KEY=your-antigravity-api-key

# ===========================================
# Frontend Configuration (Vite)
# ===========================================
# Add these to your frontend .env file:

# VITE_DASHBOARD_API_KEY=your-dashboard-api-key-here
# VITE_DASHBOARD_API_URL=https://digitallydefined-os-backend.vercel.app
# VITE_CHAT_API_URL=https://digitallydefined-os-backend.vercel.app/api/hermes
# VITE_HERMES_GATEWAY_URL=https://digitallydefined-os-backend.vercel.app/api/hermes

# ===========================================
# Hermes MCP Configuration
# ===========================================
# The Hermes MCP server will automatically use the same OMNIROUTE_API_KEY
# and OMNIROUTE_BASE_URL from the backend environment.

# No additional configuration needed - Hermes agents will use OmniRoute
# through the modules/omniroute.py client.

# ===========================================
# Testing
# ===========================================
# To test your OmniRoute configuration:

# 1. Verify the API key is set:
#    echo $OMNIROUTE_API_KEY

# 2. Test with curl:
#    curl -X POST https://omniroute.ai/v1/chat/completions \
#      -H "Authorization: Bearer $OMNIROUTE_API_KEY" \
#      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#      -d '{"model":"openai/gpt-4o-mini","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Hello"}]}'

# 3. Test the backend endpoint:
#    curl -X POST https://digitallydefined-os-backend.vercel.app/api?action=hermes \
#      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#      -H "x-api-key: $DASHBOARD_API_KEY" \
#      -d '{"message":"Hello, Hermes!"}'

# ===========================================
# Migration Guide
# ===========================================
# If you're migrating from direct API calls:

# 1. Set OMNIROUTE_API_KEY in your environment
# 2. Remove or comment out old API keys (GROQ_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, etc.)
# 3. Deploy the backend with the new omniroute.js client
# 4. Test all AI endpoints:
#    - /api?action=hermes
#    - /api?action=brain.brief
#    - /api?action=automation.sync
# 5. Monitor logs for any errors
# 6. Once confirmed working, you can safely remove old API keys

# ===========================================
# Troubleshooting
# ===========================================
# Issue: "OMNIROUTE_API_KEY not configured"
# Solution: Set the OMNIROUTE_API_KEY environment variable

# Issue: "All OmniRoute models failed"
# Solution: Check OMNIROUTE_BASE_URL is correct, verify API key is valid

# Issue: Rate limiting errors
# Solution: Add fallback models (OMNIROUTE_FALLBACK_MODEL_1, OMNIROUTE_FALLBACK_MODEL_2)

# Issue: Timeout errors
# Solution: Increase timeout in the client (default: 60s) or check network connectivity